{
  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset: ONE independent hand-painted game run animation sprite of the same Ghost Script Calligrapher Boy. Input 1 is the approved FRONT/S-facing identity, anatomy, costume and camera reference. Input 2 is original identity portrait. Input 3 is PRIMARY approved clean polished Taoist chibi painting style; borrow rendering only, no UI or lettering. This is new animation anatomy, not recolored idle.\nCharacter faces straight SOUTH toward viewer, full frontal head, both amber eyes, not a three-quarter side turn. Native square at least 1024x1024, transparent alpha background. Fixed orthographic camera: head width 34% of canvas, body center x50%, same scale as input1, nominal ground line y92%. All props/feet/ribbon inside generous margin. Torso leans slightly toward viewer for forward travel.\nPreserve short brown straight tousled hair/high bun, yin-yang ornament, plain teal ribbon tails, jade forehead diamond, amber eyes; charcoal gold-cloud short robe with ivory lining, jade belt yin-yang buckle, FULL LENGTH dark trousers reaching black/gold boots. No bare calf, no skin below waist, no white socks. Anatomical RIGHT hand is on image LEFT and grips brush; anatomical LEFT hand is on image RIGHT and grips blank ivory hanging scroll. Do not swap hands. Exactly two pale cyan ink spirits travel beside scroll. One small legitimate teal brush tassel only at top handle butt, never near bristles. Scroll one yin-yang teal tassel, no ornament at hair ribbon tips. Clear five-finger grip and connected wrists, exactly two arms/two hands/two legs/two boots. Smooth clean alpha edges, no white/pink/cyan fringe, no floating specks. No floor shadow, particles, magic trails, texts or extra objects.\nPOSE: run/S/03 RIGHT LOW SUPPORT / LEFT PASSING. RIGHT leg on image LEFT is planted almost vertically beneath hip and visibly bent at knee for weight support. Pelvis and head lower together by 20 pixels, head scale unchanged. LEFT leg on image RIGHT has swung beside and slightly ahead of support knee, knee flexed 35 degrees maximum, left boot lifted low, not chest high. RIGHT brush shoulder rotates forward, gripping hand passes waist toward low chest; LEFT scroll shoulder rotates backward, hand passes waist toward rear hip. Distinct asymmetric leg anatomy; this is lowest running compression, not a lunge or a high knee pose.",
